# reports_to is a hint for tc cards, tc health and the board, never a route.

def unread_count(name):
    """How many unread messages mail/to-<name>/ holds; 0 with no inbox.

    Unlike unread(), it never creates the inbox. SHARED fix round 1
    (Claude Opus 5.5, unreviewed): only a real folder counts (lstat), so a
    linked inbox holds 0, as send, read and wait refuse it; and only
    regular files count (message_files), as `tc read` moves only those.
    SHARED fix round 2 (Claude Opus 5.5, unreviewed): an entry lstat
    cannot reach is not counted, and an inbox this user cannot list
    holds 0 here (message_files), never a traceback. SHARED fix round 4
    (Claude Opus 5.5, unreviewed): the audit's LOW-7. So this count's own
    callers get a silent 0 for such an inbox: cmd_join (the ring marker),
    cmd_card (its refusal over unread mail) and deliver_codex (the ring
    decision), as the handoff's pause 8 says. Peek, read and wait say
    they could not list it (inbox_messages), log names it (cmd_log), and
    mailbox_summary reports the count as unknown.

    @interacts  lstats mail/to-<name>; lists it and lstats each *.md
                entry. Writes nothing.
    @deps       real_folder, message_files; MAIL.
    @complexity O(u) over u *.md entries in the inbox (single digits).
    @alloc      two lists, freed on return.
    """
    box = MAIL / f"to-{name}"
    return len(message_files(box)[0]) if real_folder(box) else 0


